cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this talk pack, please cite it as below."
title: "A Practitioner's Guide to Graphs — talk pack"
abstract: >-
  Companion pack for the talk "A Practitioner's Guide to Graphs — how to make
  your AI applications smarter, cheaper and more reliable" (AI Engineer World's
  Fair 2026, Graph Track). A practitioner narrative — bad graph to good graph
  to payoff — with a runnable graphtools library and offline-replayable
  notebooks covering schema-first extraction, ontology in the prompt, entity
  matching, and the graph algorithms (Personalised PageRank, shortest path,
  exact subgraph matching) that make graphs worth it.
type: software
authors:
